      "ordinal": 1,
      "exactText": "### Layer 1 — atomic component\n\nSmall reusable pieces with their own stable local interface:\n\n- PCB carriers;\n- processors / IC packages;\n- resistors, capacitors, diodes and transistors;\n- fuses and regulators;\n- switches and potentiometers;\n- headers, wire connectors, terminal blocks and test jacks;\n- buzzers, LEDs and inductors;\n- existing reusable fasteners, battery cells and battery contacts.\n\nAtomic components should remain independent from the device shell and should normally be instanced at scale `1,1,1`.\n\n",
      "citation": {
        "display": "docs/ELECTRONICS_MODULAR_SYSTEM.md:L28-L42",
        "handleId": "bb3ab88c78175b182c6b8f8c31ef92d10dfa1f4ac80710007a0dbf1265b6c2ac",
        "owner": "d:/dev/electronics-repair-simulator",
        "sourceRef": "docs/ELECTRONICS_MODULAR_SYSTEM.md",
        "revision": "4a5556680a4f395bdbc4e6b578d9fbc368c15483fdad6b6f57aeef3e84a5cd77",
        "rangeId": "heading-4",
        "rangeKind": "section",
        "startLine": 28,
        "endLine": 42,
        "fingerprint": "5f919b498796bea576d33e9a24f05b8b5f2fe8c3b258c90cdd36b2e59730bd59",
        "privacyClass": "project-metadata"
      }
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 2,
      "exactText": "A module owns the placement of its atomics, but those atomics retain source lineage and detachable identities when the repair loop may expose them.",
      "citation": {
        "display": "docs/ELECTRONICS_MODULAR_SYSTEM.md:L55-L55",
        "handleId": "8fc026e6912cf0fe6a43d2da25673c723a2c22ae20ce36a88daf466a073e2098",
