        "endLine": 55,
        "fingerprint": "0f170c53bb8cac2ea60ebaf8d4a79b6158a9ff04452b61cf6cb8e7298bab144c",
        "privacyClass": "project-metadata"
      }
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 3,
      "exactText": "### Layer 3 — serviceable assembly\n\nThe device-specific interior and shell contract:\n\n- covers;\n- screw interfaces;\n- PCB/module mount points;\n- battery cradle/contact placement;\n- cable routing;\n- optical/mechanical interfaces;\n- removal order.\n\nThe serviceable assembly decides which reusable pieces are instantiated and which device-specific geometry must be derived or created.\n\n",
      "citation": {
        "display": "docs/ELECTRONICS_MODULAR_SYSTEM.md:L57-L70",
        "handleId": "f9305df9fb20c8416db886b8955eb38a22951663cb06898bfca63615f5c81f0e",
